// api/tsconfig.json — the @vercel/node nearest-tsconfig resolution pin (T052 follow-up, W-3i).
//
// THE W-3i LESSON (deploy-triggered failure dpl_Ajr2KCQmT9axQGwDEcvpBkLFc4aV):
// after the W-3h discovery shim made Vercel FIND this function, the build's
// TypeScript typecheck still failed — @vercel/node resolves compiler options
// from the tsconfig.json NEAREST the function entry (walking up from
// api/router.ts), and with no tsconfig.json in api/ its default synthesis
// ran moduleResolution "nodenext". Under nodenext every extensionless
// relative import is an error (TS2835: "Relative import paths need explicit
// file extensions in ECMAScript imports... Did you mean './identity.js'?"),
// and the frozen services/api sources — plus this shim's own re-export —
// are written extensionless: the style the whole repo already typechecks
// green under (tsconfig.base.json: moduleResolution "Bundler"). The
// TS2339/TS2322 errors in the build log were cascades — services/api's
// types collapsed first, so every consumer of them lost its types.
//
// THE LAW (pinned by deploy/vercel/vercel.test.ts): NEVER add file
// extensions to the frozen services/api imports to satisfy a build tool —
// pin the resolution instead. This file is the nearest tsconfig on the
// entry's walk-up path, so @vercel/node reads THESE options: the repo base
// extended with the same Bundler resolution the root typecheck proves
// green over this exact entry + import-closure graph.
{
  "extends": "../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "Bundler"
  },
  "include": ["./**/*.ts", "../deploy/vercel/**/*.ts", "../services/api/**/*.ts"]
}
